# tau_eb_falsifier/2lpt0_highz_taueb_off.env
# Track C tau_eb high-z falsifier — ARM A (ISOLATION).
#
# CONTEXT: the 2LPT-0 V1 production baseline (gl_prod_2lpt0_v1_20260526) already
# ran tau_eb ON with the *null* objective. The DLA-tier NHI bias (+0.038 dex,
# measured from baseline processed h5) therefore PERSISTS *with* tau_eb-null on.
# This arm flips tau_eb OFF on the same high-z up-migration subset to isolate
# what the current null-objective tau_eb is doing to the bias:
#   - if bias gets WORSE with OFF  => null tau_eb already helps (lever works);
#   - if bias is UNCHANGED          => null tau_eb does nothing here (need a
#                                      stronger lever, see ARM B / kernel fix).
#
# IDENTICAL to 2lpt0_gl_v1.env EXCEPT: ENABLE_TAU_EB=0 + restricted to the
# high-z host TID subset (EXTERNAL_TID_LIST). No inference-code change.
source "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/../2lpt0_gl_v1.env"

ENABLE_TAU_EB=0
RUN_NAME="gl_taueb_falsifier_2lpt0_highz_OFF_${RUN_DATE}"
OUTDIR="${GL_OUTPUT_ROOT}/${RUN_NAME}/outputs/"

# High-z up-migration DLA-host subset (903 TIDs: truth NHI in [20.1,20.6],
# z_DLA>3.0, z_qso>3.1; built by build_highz_subset.py). Spans sorted level2
# index [0,186) — launch with --start 0 --end 186.
EXTERNAL_TID_LIST="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")" && pwd)/highz_upmig_hosts.txt"
